perience with recursive functions","comments":4,"created_at":"2024-02-28T16:07:21Z"},{"number":288,"title":"nevergrad import fails when profiler is active","comments":4,"created_at":"2024-01-18T18:58:57Z"},{"number":347,"title":"Timeline view is difficult to scroll around on","comments":3,"created_at":"2024-10-14T19:00:35Z"}],"discussions":[{"number":469,"title":"Would it be possible to publish pre-compiled wheels for Python 3.15?","comments":1,"category":"Q&A","created_at":"2026-11-11T16:29:26Z"},{"number":438,"title":"Python 3.15: Tachyon","comments":1,"category":"General","created_at":"2026-04-20T15:45:50Z"},{"number":433,"title":"how to display in more ways?","comments":0,"category":"Q&A","created_at":"2026-04-01T08:25:36Z"},{"number":424,"title":"Relationship between pyinstrument and Tachyon (profiling.sampling)","comments":0,"category":"Q&A","created_at":"2026-02-17T18:52:19Z"},{"number":399,"title":"Thanks","comments":1,"category":"General","created_at":"2025-09-24T06:05:40Z"},{"number":378,"title":"possible to sample python cpp extensions ...?","comments":1,"category":"General","created_at":"2025-03-25T22:08:38Z"},{"number":375,"title":"Visually inspecting results from a database or easily accessing instrumentation","comments":0,"category":"General","created_at":"2024-10-07T18:32:53Z"},{"number":376,"title":"Pyinstruments creates long intervals with no profiling","comments":0,"category":"General","created_at":"2024-10-05T21:29:56Z"}],"latest_release":{"name":"","tag":"v5.1.3","published_at":"2026-07-29T17:11:13Z","body":"-    Fixed Django middleware so `PYINSTRUMENT_SHOW_CALLBACK` is respected when `PYINSTRUMENT_PROFILE_DIR` is configured, allowing profiles to be selectively written to disk (#452).\r\n-    Fixed Jupyter’s `%%pyinstrument` magic so console-specific render options, including `time=percent_of_total`, `flat`, `short_mode`, `color`, and Unicode settings, are correctly applied to text output (#446).\r\n-    Fixed long program and command names overflowing the header in HTML reports. Long names now wrap cleanly (#449).\r\n-    Added context-manager type annotations so type checkers correctly infer profile as a Profiler in with Profiler() as profile: blocks (#445).\r\n-    Expanded wheel-building coverage to include CPython prereleases and GraalPy (#442).\r\n-    Replaced the deprecated vendored appdirs implementation with simpler internal platform-specific user-data-directory handling (#451).\r\n-    Updated build tooling and dependencies, including cibuildwheel and GitHub Actions.\r\n","is_prerelease":false},"readme":true,"readme_zh":false,"news":[],"stale":false,"snapshot_at":"2026-11-14T08:50:43Z","history_start":"2026-09-06"}